WIRE.md §8.1, CODEGEN.md §2.1 (DECISIONS 229): an emit json out list of files is in file mode, so it writes exactly one value; the list is judged once, by its first entry.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// One.
let one: Int = 1
/// Two.
let two: Int = 2

emit json { out: ["@sovcommon/a.json", "@features/a.json"] }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8150]  a/a.canon:8:6
  emit json out "@sovcommon/a.json" is a file but values has 2 elements

